// Precomputed particle target coordinates for the five reference
// illustrations (Halftone Shell, Monstera Leaf, Dandelion, Galaxy, Dotwork Flower).
//
// Generated offline in two layers (see work/sample_final.py in project
// history for the pipeline):
//  1. Structure points, traced along the artwork's own contours
//     (outer silhouette, and meaningful internal holes/segments — a leaf's splits,
//     pupil, the splits and midrib of the Monstera leaf) via OpenCV contour
//     detection, resampled to even arc-length spacing. This is what
//     gives recognisable hard structure instead of relying on density
//     sampling alone to accidentally suggest the right shape.
//  2. Fill points, the same variable-density blue-noise (Poisson-disk)
//     sampling as before, seeded with the structure points so the
//     organic texture never lands on top of a traced boundary.
//
// Each entry: `aspect` is the illustration's content-bounding-box
// width/height (used to fit it into the canvas without distortion —
// see fitIllustration in compositions.js), and `points` is a flat
// [x0,y0,x1,y1,...] array normalized to that bounding box, pre-shuffled
// so the first N*2 values are themselves a valid representative
// subsample for any particle count up to the full pool.

export const FEATHER_ASPECT = 0.8088

// Structured feather — 2000 points, constructed from the reference's own
// anatomy rather than tone-sampled, so every dot carries part of the form:
//  - shaft: a spline through the reference's dark quill, which sweeps up into
//    its dark lower ridge, then fades through the pale vane toward the apex;
//  - split-edge ridges: the reference's dark lobe edges (left arcs, upper
//    cleft, base fringe), blue-noise stippled at a tight spacing;
//  - barbs: rows marched out from the shaft on both sides, swept toward the
//    apex and clipped to the reference silhouette (notches preserved), with
//    spacing tight near the shaft, widening to the edge, and density thinned
//    in the reference's lighter regions (dark lower-left -> light upper-right).
// Min-distance filtering keeps spacing intentional; jitter keeps it organic.
// Prefix-ordered by weighted sample elimination (shaft/edge dots favoured) so
// any prefix still reads as a feather on small screens.
